{
  "format": "hm-conformance",
  "version": 1,
  "subject": "hm-learn-scheduling",
  "description": "Spaced repetition (learn-sdk ADR 0004): FSRS-7 without fuzzing (\"fsrs\", with optional desiredRetention and weights), and the fake scheduler from @hussmartinez/learn-sdk/testing (\"fake\"). input.start begins with a new item's state at that time, or input.state continues from a stored one; input.reviews are applied in order. expected is every state in turn with its due time, the new item's first, or the rejection. Times are milliseconds since the Unix epoch. FSRS-7 states hold computed floats, compared within the case's tolerance.",
